#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# cyclotomic

#% text
# `cyclotomic(k, x)` gives the k-th cyclotomic polynomial in x, whose roots are the primitive k-th roots of unity.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is computed as the product of `(x^d - 1)^moebius_mu(k/d)` over the divisors d of k (Moebius inversion of x^k - 1 = product of the cyclotomic polynomials of the divisors).

#% item
# x may be a number: `cyclotomic(k, 1)` is p for k a power of the prime p and 1 for other k > 1.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
cyclotomic(5, x)
#% output
#= 1 + x + x^2 + x^3 + x^4

#% cell
cyclotomic(12, x)
#% output
#= 1 - x^2 + x^4

#% cell
table(cyclotomic(k, 1), [k, 2, 20])
#% output
#= [2, 3, 2, 5, 1, 7, 2, 3, 1, 11, 1, 13, 1, 1, 2, 17, 1, 19, 1]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `factor`, `moebius_mu`, `divisors`
